    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The GATT Bibliography was first published in March 1954 and covered the\r\nperiod from 1947 to the end of 1953. The First Supplement covered the period from January 1954 to June 1955. The Second Supplement covered the period from June 1955 to June 1956; the Third Supplement from June 1956 to August 1957; the Fourth Supplement from August 1957 to July 1958; The Fifth Supplement from August 1958 to July 1959; the Sixth Supplement from July 1959 to July I960; the Seventh Supplement from July I960 to July 1961; the Eighth Supplement from July 196! to July 1962; the Ninth Supplement from July l962 to July 1963; the Tenth Supplement covers the period from August 1963 to December 1964.\r\n\r\nAmong the main events referred to in the Tenth Supplement are:\r\n- the twenty-first session of the Contracting Parties, held at Geneva\r\nfrom 24 February to 20 March 1964;\r\n- the meetings of--the GATT Council of Representatives;\r\n- the opening of the Kennedy-round of trade negotiations at ministerial\r\nlevel on 4 May 1964;\r\n- the US - EEC chicken war and the GATT arbitration, August - November\r\n1963;\r\n- the special session of the Contracting Parties in November 1964, at\r\nwhich was completed the new Part TV of the General Agreement, entitled\r\n\"Trade and Development\";\r\n- the-publication of the GATT annual reports: \"international Trade 1962\" and \"International Trade 1963\".\r\n\r\nThe GATT Bibliography and its Supplements do not include the publications of the GATT secretariat.",
